'''R3-T2''', or just '''R3''', was an [[R3-series astromech droid]] with [[Color|red]], blue, and white paneling. They lived in [[Mos Eisley]] [[spaceport]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] and in [[9 BBY]] stood in one of the streets when a [[Scythe (Phi-class)|transport]] carrying three [[Inquisitorius|Inquisitors]] landed nearby. In [[1 BBY]], the droid passed by a [[X-34 landspeeder]] as they moved along [[Corporations Road]] in the spaceport.

==Biography==
R3-T2, also known as just R3, was an unaffiliated<ref name="CGttSWG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> [[R3-series astromech droid]] resident of the [[spaceport]] of [[Mos Eisley]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="IncrediBuilds" /> Over the [[Standard year|years]], the [[droid]] had several owners who kept R3-T2 in order using parts [[Scavenger|scavenged]] from members of the [[Jawa]] [[species]].<ref name="CGttSWG" />

In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="KenobiDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates {{Kenobi|Part I}} to [[9 BBY]].</ref> the droid was stood among the crowds on one of Mos Eisley's streets when the [[transport]]<ref name="KenobiI">{{Kenobi|Part I}}</ref> [[Scythe (Phi-class)|''Scythe'']]<ref name="Scythe">{{LEGOWeb|url=en-us/product/inquisitor-transport-scythe-75336|text=Inquisitor Transport ''Scythe''}}</ref> flew overhead and landed nearby to allow three [[Sith]] [[Inquisitorius|Inquisitors]] to disembark, although the droid did not turn to face the Inquisitors with the rest of the crowd.<ref name="KenobiI" />

In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]'' dates the [[secret mission to Tatooine]] to [[1 BBY]].</ref> R3-T2 was rolling down<ref name="ANH" /> [[Corporations Road]] in Mos Eisley when an [[X-34 landspeeder]] carrying the locals [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and Skywalker's droids, [[R2-D2]] and [[C-3PO]], passed them. A recklessly [[pilot]]ed [[Flare-S swoop]]<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> then caused a [[ronto]] to rear up in front of R3-T2, causing a Jawa to fall from the ronto's back in front of the droid. The [[astromech droid]] later passed by the same [[landspeeder]] again outside [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]].<ref name="ANH" />

==Characteristics==
Standing 1.09 [[meter]]s tall,<ref name="Height" /> R3-T2 had a black [[sensor]] on their [[Color|red]] dome and white-and-blue paneling on their chassis.<ref name="ANH" /> They were part of the [[R-series]] manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]].<ref name="IncrediBuilds" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:R3-T2-Ronto-ANH.png|thumb|right|300px|R3-T2 (far right) first appeared in ''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope''.]]
R3-T2 first appeared in the [[1977]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="ANH" /> The droid's scene was shot between [[April 2]] and [[April 4]], [[1976]] on location in [[Wikipedia:Djerba|Djerba]], [[Wikipedia:Tunisia|Tunisia]].<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Star Wars]]''</ref> The droid was recreated based on the original for the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series, with the crew using R3-T2 as the model's identifier.<ref name="KenobiITrivia">{{SW|url=obi-wan-kenobi-part-i-trivia-gallery|text=Part I Trivia Gallery &#124; Obi-Wan Kenobi}} {{C|Slide 1}}</ref> R3-T2's scene was shot on the fourteenth day of shooting for the series<ref name="Return">''[[Obi-Wan Kenobi: A Jedi's Return]]''</ref> and the droid then appeared in the show's [[Part I|first episode]],<ref name="KenobiI" /> which aired on [[May 27]], [[2022]].<ref name="Episode 1 Premiere">{{Twitter|obiwankenobi|status/1530019678562549760|''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]''|date=2022-05-27|quote=The time for #ObiWanKenobi has arrived&hellip;early. Start streaming the first two episodes on @DisneyPlus TONIGHT at 9PM PT.|archivedate=20220527053945}}</ref>

In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the droid was first identified in the [[2016]] reference book written by [[Michael Kogge]] included in the ''[[Star Wars: R2-D2 Deluxe Book and Model Set]]''.<ref name="IncrediBuilds" /> The designation originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where they were first used on the [http://www.starwarsccg.org/cardlists/images/starwars/SpecialEdition-Light/large/r3t2.gif "R3-T2 (Arthree-Teetoo)" card] in the ''[[Special Edition Limited]]'' expansion set of the [[Star Wars Customizable Card Game|''Star Wars'' Customizable Card Game]], which was released by [[Decipher]] in [[1998]].<ref name="CCG">{{CCG|set=Special Edition Limited|cardname=R3-T2 (Arthree-Teetoo)}}</ref>

A [[LEGO]] figure of R3-T2 was created for the [[2018]] set "75198 Tatooine Battle Pack."<ref name="LEGO">{{LEGOCite|num=75198|name=Tatooine Battle Pack}}</ref> Images of this figure were re-used in the [[2023]] non-canon reference book ''[[LEGO Star Wars Galaxy Mission]]'' to represent the separate character [[R2-Z2C]]. The book was written by [[Julia March]] with LEGO models by [[Rod Gillies]].<ref name="Galaxy">''[[LEGO Star Wars Galaxy Mission]]''</ref>

